:: Guesthouse \[Event\] - male on female {"position":"336,1079","size":"100,100"}
<h1 class="ptitle">GUEST HOUSE</h1>

<<if ($tmpEvent.wifeGuestIdxs ?? []).length > 0 && typeof $randEvent === 'undefined'>>
	<<set _wifeIdx = $tmpEvent.wifeGuestIdxs[0]>>
	<<set _wife = $guests[_wifeIdx]>>
	<<set _selectedFemale = $guests[$tmpEvent.femaleGuestIds[0]]>>
	<<set _husband = $guests[$tmpEvent.maleGuestIds[0]]>>
	<<set _wifeLikesGuys = (_wife.likesGuys ?? true)>>
	<<set _wifeLikesGirls = (_wife.likesGirls ?? false)>>
	<<set _wifeDie = random(1, 100)>>
	<<if _wifeLikesGuys && _wifeLikesGirls>>
		<<if _wifeDie <= 20>>
			<<set _wifeOutcome = 'leaves_bi'>>
		<<elseif _wifeDie <= 50>>
			<<set _wifeOutcome = 'stays_bi'>>
		<<else>>
			<<set _wifeOutcome = 'joins'>>
		<</if>>
	<<elseif _wifeLikesGuys>>
		<<set _wifeOutcome = _wifeDie <= 30 ? 'stays_straight' : 'leaves_straight'>>
	<<elseif _wifeLikesGirls>>
		<<if _wifeDie <= 20>>
			<<set _wifeOutcome = 'joins'>>
		<<elseif _wifeDie <= 50>>
			<<set _wifeOutcome = 'stays_lesbian'>>
		<<else>>
			<<set _wifeOutcome = 'leaves_lesbian'>>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		<<set _wifeOutcome = 'leaves_neither'>>
	<</if>>
	<br />
	<<if _wifeOutcome === 'leaves_bi'>>
		His wife, <<=setup.displayName(_wife)>>, is already at the doorway when you get there. She looks at <<=setup.displayName(_husband)>> and <<=setup.displayName(_selectedFemale)>> together — takes it in — and lets out a slow breath through her nose. Something in her expression tightens for a second and then closes off. She pulls the door closed softly on her way out and doesn't say anything, and her footsteps down the corridor are quiet and fast.
		<br /><br />
		<<sayNpc _wife>>
			<<set _reactionOptions = [
				"I know when I'm not needed.",
				"It should have been me.",
				"I would have been better than her.",
				"Fine. I get it.",
				"I hope she's worth it."
			]>>
			<<=setup.getRandomElement(_reactionOptions)>>
		<</sayNpc>>
	<<elseif _wifeOutcome === 'stays_bi'>>
		His wife, <<=setup.displayName(_wife)>>, is leaning against the far wall when you arrive, watching <<=setup.displayName(_husband)>> and <<=setup.displayName(_selectedFemale)>> with obvious interest. No jealousy in it — she looks more like a spectator who got a good seat than someone who was wronged. She stays right where she is, eyes on the two of them, and when the encounter starts she doesn't move, doesn't look away, and doesn't acknowledge you.
		<br /><br />
		<<sayNpc _wife>>
			<<set _reactionOptions = [
				"Sometimes it's more fun just to watch.",
				"Let's see just how good she is.",
				"I wouldn't mind her for myself.",
				"I could get used to this arrangement.",
				"Don't worry about me. I'm enjoying the show."
			]>>
			<<=setup.getRandomElement(_reactionOptions)>>
		<</sayNpc>>
	<<elseif _wifeOutcome === 'joins'>>
		His wife, <<=setup.displayName(_wife)>>, is there before you are. She looks at <<=setup.displayName(_selectedFemale)>>, looks at <<=setup.displayName(_husband)>>, and steps inside. She goes straight to <<=setup.displayName(_selectedFemale)>> — no hesitation, hands first — and <<=setup.displayName(_husband)>> comes in behind her and closes the door. All three of them are into it from the start. It works without instruction.
		<br /><br />
		<<sayNpc _wife>>
			<<set _reactionOptions = [
				"Let me show you how he likes it.",
				"Why don't we enjoy her together?",
				"That looks fun. Room for a third?",
				"Don't start without me.",
				"I can share if you can."
			]>>
			<<=setup.getRandomElement(_reactionOptions)>>
		<</sayNpc>>
	<<elseif _wifeOutcome === 'stays_straight'>>
		His wife, <<=setup.displayName(_wife)>>, is inside the door when you arrive — rigid, jaw set, arms at her sides. She watches <<=setup.displayName(_husband)>> and <<=setup.displayName(_selectedFemale)>> with controlled blankness, the kind that costs something to maintain. She knows she doesn't get to leave. She stays for all of it, eyes forward, and by the end the effort of holding herself together has written itself into her posture.
		<br /><br />
		<<sayNpc _wife>>
			<<set _reactionOptions = [
				"Go ahead. Try and enjoy yourselves.",
				"Let's see if she's as good as I am.",
				"I want to see if he's any different when it's not me.",
				"I'll be right here. Don't let me get in the way.",
				"Fine. I'll watch."
			]>>
			<<=setup.getRandomElement(_reactionOptions)>>
		<</sayNpc>>
	<<elseif _wifeOutcome === 'leaves_straight'>>
		His wife, <<=setup.displayName(_wife)>>, gets there first. She sees <<=setup.displayName(_husband)>> and <<=setup.displayName(_selectedFemale)>> and her posture goes tight — a quick involuntary thing she can't quite help. She doesn't make a scene. She turns and walks, and her footsteps going away are faster than they were coming in. <<=setup.displayName(_husband)>> watches her go for a second, then turns back to <<=setup.displayName(_selectedFemale)>>.
		<br /><br />
		<<sayNpc _wife>>
			<<set _reactionOptions = [
				"I know when I'm not needed.",
				"It should have been me.",
				"I would have been better than her.",
				"Fine. I get it.",
				"I hope she's worth it."
			]>>
			<<=setup.getRandomElement(_reactionOptions)>>
		<</sayNpc>>
	<<elseif _wifeOutcome === 'stays_lesbian'>>
		His wife, <<=setup.displayName(_wife)>>, walks straight past <<=setup.displayName(_husband)>> — he's not why she stayed — and finds a clear angle on <<=setup.displayName(_selectedFemale)>>. Her attention fixes there and doesn't move. She watches <<=setup.displayName(_selectedFemale)>> directly and doesn't bother making it less obvious. <<=setup.displayName(_husband)>> she barely registers; when the encounter starts, he might as well not be in the room.
		<br /><br />
		<<sayNpc _wife>>
			<<set _reactionOptions = [
				"Sometimes it's more fun just to watch.",
				"Let's see just how good she is.",
				"I wouldn't mind her for myself.",
				"Go ahead. I'll be right here.",
				"I'm just here for her, honestly."
			]>>
			<<=setup.getRandomElement(_reactionOptions)>>
		<</sayNpc>>
	<<elseif _wifeOutcome === 'leaves_lesbian'>>
		His wife, <<=setup.displayName(_wife)>>, glances in, sees <<=setup.displayName(_husband)>> and <<=setup.displayName(_selectedFemale)>>, and something in her face loosens — the kind of relief you get when a problem handles itself. She turns and walks, easy, unhurried, and doesn't look back. In the room, <<=setup.displayName(_husband)>> and <<=setup.displayName(_selectedFemale)>> are already at it.
		<br /><br />
		<<sayNpc _wife>>
			<<set _reactionOptions = [
				"I'll leave you two to it.",
				"You two have fun.",
				"Better her than me.",
				"Don't mind me. I'm heading out.",
				"Carry on. I wasn't going to get involved anyway."
			]>>
			<<=setup.getRandomElement(_reactionOptions)>>
		<</sayNpc>>
	<<else>>
		His wife, <<=setup.displayName(_wife)>>, looks in at <<=setup.displayName(_husband)>> and <<=setup.displayName(_selectedFemale)>> and goes. No visible reaction. She has somewhere else to be.
		<br /><br />
		<<sayNpc _wife>>
			<<set _reactionOptions = [
				"I'll leave you two to it.",
				"You two have fun.",
				"Don't mind me. I'm heading out.",
				"Carry on. I wasn't going to get involved anyway.",
				"Enjoy yourselves."
			]>>
			<<=setup.getRandomElement(_reactionOptions)>>
		<</sayNpc>>
	<</if>>
	<br /><br />
	<<if _wifeOutcome === 'joins'>>
		<<link 'Continue'>>
			<<set $guests[$tmpEvent.maleGuestIds[0]].happy = Math.min(100, ($guests[$tmpEvent.maleGuestIds[0]].happy ?? 50) + 5)>>
			<<set _wife.corruption = Math.min(100, (_wife.corruption ?? 0) + 3)>>
			<<set $guests[$tmpEvent.maleGuestIds[0]].corruption = Math.min(100, ($guests[$tmpEvent.maleGuestIds[0]].corruption ?? 0) + 1)>>
			<<set $tmpEvent = {
				maleGuestIds: $tmpEvent.maleGuestIds,
				femaleGuestIds: _wifeIdx !== undefined ? [$tmpEvent.femaleGuestIds[0], _wifeIdx] : $tmpEvent.femaleGuestIds
			}>>
			<<goto 'Guesthouse [Event] - male on females'>>
		<</link>>
		<<linkdesc>>+5 happy, +1 corruption to <<=setup.displayName(_husband)>>; +3 corruption to <<=setup.displayName(_wife)>><</linkdesc>>
	<<elseif _wifeOutcome === 'stays_bi' || _wifeOutcome === 'stays_lesbian'>>
		<<link 'Continue'>>
			<<set _wife.happy = Math.min(100, (_wife.happy ?? 50) + 3)>>
			<<set _wife.corruption = Math.min(100, (_wife.corruption ?? 0) + 2)>>
			<<set $guests[$tmpEvent.maleGuestIds[0]].happy = Math.min(100, ($guests[$tmpEvent.maleGuestIds[0]].happy ?? 50) + 3)>>
			<<run delete $tmpEvent.wifeGuestIdxs>>
			<<goto 'Guesthouse [Event] - male on female'>>
		<</link>>
		<<linkdesc>>+3 happy, +2 corruption to <<=setup.displayName(_wife)>>; +3 happy to <<=setup.displayName(_husband)>><</linkdesc>>
	<<elseif _wifeOutcome === 'stays_straight'>>
		<<link 'Continue'>>
			<<set _wife.happy = Math.max(0, (_wife.happy ?? 50) - 5)>>
			<<set _wife.corruption = Math.min(100, (_wife.corruption ?? 0) + 4)>>
			<<set $guests[$tmpEvent.maleGuestIds[0]].happy = Math.max(0, ($guests[$tmpEvent.maleGuestIds[0]].happy ?? 50) - 3)>>
			<<set $guests[$tmpEvent.maleGuestIds[0]].corruption = Math.min(100, ($guests[$tmpEvent.maleGuestIds[0]].corruption ?? 0) + 1)>>
			<<run delete $tmpEvent.wifeGuestIdxs>>
			<<goto 'Guesthouse [Event] - male on female'>>
		<</link>>
		<<linkdesc>>−5 happy, +4 corruption to <<=setup.displayName(_wife)>>; −3 happy, +1 corruption to <<=setup.displayName(_husband)>><</linkdesc>>
	<<elseif _wifeOutcome === 'leaves_bi' || _wifeOutcome === 'leaves_straight'>>
		<<link 'Continue'>>
			<<set _wife.happy = Math.max(0, (_wife.happy ?? 50) - 5)>>
			<<run delete $tmpEvent.wifeGuestIdxs>>
			<<goto 'Guesthouse [Event] - male on female'>>
		<</link>>
		<<linkdesc>>−5 happy to <<=setup.displayName(_wife)>><</linkdesc>>
	<<else>>
		<<link 'Continue'>>
			<<set _wife.happy = Math.min(100, (_wife.happy ?? 50) + 3)>>
			<<run delete $tmpEvent.wifeGuestIdxs>>
			<<goto 'Guesthouse [Event] - male on female'>>
		<</link>>
		<<linkdesc>>+3 happy to <<=setup.displayName(_wife)>><</linkdesc>>
	<</if>>
<<elseif ($tmpEvent.husbandGuestIdxs ?? []).length > 0 && typeof $randEvent === 'undefined'>>
	<<set _husbandIdx = $tmpEvent.husbandGuestIdxs[0]>>
	<<set _husband = $guests[_husbandIdx]>>
	<<set _wifeFemale = $guests[$tmpEvent.femaleGuestIds[0]]>>
	<<set _selectedMale = $guests[$tmpEvent.maleGuestIds[0]]>>
	<<set _husbandLikesGuys = (_husband.likesGuys ?? false)>>
	<<set _husbandLikesGirls = (_husband.likesGirls ?? true)>>
	<<set _husbandDie = random(1, 100)>>
	<<if _husbandLikesGirls && _husbandLikesGuys>>
		<<if _husbandDie <= 20>>
			<<set _husbandOutcome = 'leaves_bi'>>
		<<elseif _husbandDie <= 50>>
			<<set _husbandOutcome = 'stays_bi'>>
		<<else>>
			<<set _husbandOutcome = 'joins_bi'>>
		<</if>>
	<<elseif _husbandLikesGirls>>
		<<if setup.percentageChance((_husband.sub ?? 0) * 2)>>
			<<set _husbandOutcome = 'stays_straight'>>
		<<else>>
			<<set _husbandOutcome = 'leaves_straight'>>
		<</if>>
	<<elseif _husbandLikesGuys>>
		<<if _husbandDie <= 10>>
			<<set _husbandOutcome = 'joins_gay'>>
		<<elseif _husbandDie <= 40>>
			<<set _husbandOutcome = 'stays_gay'>>
		<<else>>
			<<set _husbandOutcome = 'leaves_gay'>>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		<<set _husbandOutcome = 'leaves_neither'>>
	<</if>>
	<br />
	<<if _husbandOutcome === 'leaves_bi'>>
		Her husband, <<=setup.displayName(_husband)>>, is at the doorway ahead of you. He takes in <<=setup.displayName(_wifeFemale)>> and <<=setup.displayName(_selectedMale)>> — one look, quick and clear — and his expression tightens. His eyes find <<=setup.displayName(_wifeFemale)>> for a moment and then he decides not to do anything with that, and turns and walks. He keeps it together all the way down the corridor.
		<br /><br />
		<<sayNpc _husband>>
			<<set _reactionOptions = [
				"I know when I'm not needed.",
				"It should have been me.",
				"I would have been better than him.",
				"Fine. I get it.",
				"I hope he's worth it."
			]>>
			<<=setup.getRandomElement(_reactionOptions)>>
		<</sayNpc>>
	<<elseif _husbandOutcome === 'stays_bi'>>
		Her husband, <<=setup.displayName(_husband)>>, is already in the room when you arrive, positioned along the wall, watching <<=setup.displayName(_wifeFemale)>> and <<=setup.displayName(_selectedMale)>> with clear interest. Not resentful — engaged. He takes in both of them and when the encounter starts his full focus goes to the two of them. He doesn't acknowledge you when you arrive.
		<br /><br />
		<<sayNpc _husband>>
			<<set _reactionOptions = [
				"Sometimes it's more fun just to watch.",
				"Let's see just how good he is.",
				"I wouldn't mind him for myself.",
				"I could get used to this arrangement.",
				"Don't worry about me. I'm enjoying the show."
			]>>
			<<=setup.getRandomElement(_reactionOptions)>>
		<</sayNpc>>
	<<elseif _husbandOutcome === 'joins_bi'>>
		Her husband, <<=setup.displayName(_husband)>>, goes in before you do. He puts a hand on <<=setup.displayName(_wifeFemale)>>'s shoulder — familiar, easy — and when she leans into him the tension in the room drops. Then he turns to <<=setup.displayName(_selectedMale)>> and the three of them start sorting themselves out. They don't need direction. It's already working.
		<br /><br />
		<<sayNpc _husband>>
			<<set _reactionOptions = [
				"Let me show you how she likes it.",
				"Why don't we enjoy him together?",
				"That looks fun. Room for a third?",
				"Don't start without me.",
				"I can share if you can."
			]>>
			<<=setup.getRandomElement(_reactionOptions)>>
		<</sayNpc>>
	<<elseif _husbandOutcome === 'stays_straight'>>
		Her husband, <<=setup.displayName(_husband)>>, is standing just inside the door when you arrive. Too still — the way someone stands when they're working not to move. He watches <<=setup.displayName(_wifeFemale)>> and <<=setup.displayName(_selectedMale)>> with a locked jaw and careful eyes, and he knows he's not leaving. He stays for all of it, watching <<=setup.displayName(_wifeFemale)>> the whole time, and by the end the effort it took is visible in his face.
		<br /><br />
		<<sayNpc _husband>>
			<<set _reactionOptions = [
				"I'll just sit over here and stay out of the way.",
				"He's probably a lot better than me.",
				"I probably deserve this.",
				"Don't mind me. I'm not going anywhere.",
				"Fine. I'll watch."
			]>>
			<<=setup.getRandomElement(_reactionOptions)>>
		<</sayNpc>>
	<<elseif _husbandOutcome === 'leaves_straight'>>
		Her husband, <<=setup.displayName(_husband)>>, is there ahead of you. He sees <<=setup.displayName(_selectedMale)>> with <<=setup.displayName(_wifeFemale)>> — the shape of it — and goes still for a moment. Then something closes in his face and he turns and walks. No scene. He doesn't look at you on the way out. <<=setup.displayName(_wifeFemale)>> and <<=setup.displayName(_selectedMale)>> don't stop.
		<br /><br />
		<<sayNpc _husband>>
			<<set _reactionOptions = [
				"I know when I'm not needed.",
				"It should have been me.",
				"I would have been better than him.",
				"Fine. I get it.",
				"I hope he's worth it."
			]>>
			<<=setup.getRandomElement(_reactionOptions)>>
		<</sayNpc>>
	<<elseif _husbandOutcome === 'joins_gay'>>
		Her husband, <<=setup.displayName(_husband)>>, barely glances at <<=setup.displayName(_wifeFemale)>>. His eyes go to <<=setup.displayName(_selectedMale)>> and stay there — direct, decided. He steps inside, and when <<=setup.displayName(_wifeFemale)>> reads where his attention is she already understands. He doesn't explain himself. The three of them sort out their configuration, and what he came in for is obvious.
		<br /><br />
		<<sayNpc _husband>>
			<<set _reactionOptions = [
				"Room for a third?",
				"Don't start without me.",
				"That looks fun.",
				"I'll make this worth your while.",
				"Why don't we all make the most of this?"
			]>>
			<<=setup.getRandomElement(_reactionOptions)>>
		<</sayNpc>>
	<<elseif _husbandOutcome === 'stays_gay'>>
		Her husband, <<=setup.displayName(_husband)>>, moves past <<=setup.displayName(_wifeFemale)>> to where he can see <<=setup.displayName(_selectedMale)>> clearly and settles there. That's what he's here for and he doesn't obscure it — his attention locks onto <<=setup.displayName(_selectedMale)>> the way a man watches something he wants. <<=setup.displayName(_wifeFemale)>> he doesn't look at. When the encounter starts, <<=setup.displayName(_selectedMale)>> is all he's watching.
		<br /><br />
		<<sayNpc _husband>>
			<<set _reactionOptions = [
				"Sometimes it's more fun just to watch.",
				"Let's see just how good he is.",
				"I wouldn't mind him for myself.",
				"Go ahead. I'll be right here.",
				"I'm just here for him, honestly."
			]>>
			<<=setup.getRandomElement(_reactionOptions)>>
		<</sayNpc>>
	<<elseif _husbandOutcome === 'leaves_gay'>>
		Her husband, <<=setup.displayName(_husband)>>, looks in, takes a clear look at <<=setup.displayName(_wifeFemale)>> and <<=setup.displayName(_selectedMale)>>, and the set of his shoulders visibly loosens. Someone else is handling it. He steps back from the door and walks, easy pace, no hurry. In the room, <<=setup.displayName(_wifeFemale)>> and <<=setup.displayName(_selectedMale)>> continue.
		<br /><br />
		<<sayNpc _husband>>
			<<set _reactionOptions = [
				"I'll leave you two to it.",
				"You two have fun.",
				"Better him than me.",
				"Don't mind me. I'm heading out.",
				"Carry on. I wasn't going to get involved anyway."
			]>>
			<<=setup.getRandomElement(_reactionOptions)>>
		<</sayNpc>>
	<<else>>
		Her husband, <<=setup.displayName(_husband)>>, looks in at <<=setup.displayName(_wifeFemale)>> and <<=setup.displayName(_selectedMale)>> and goes. Nothing to feel about it. He just goes.
		<br /><br />
		<<sayNpc _husband>>
			<<set _reactionOptions = [
				"I'll leave you two to it.",
				"You two have fun.",
				"Don't mind me. I'm heading out.",
				"Carry on. I wasn't going to get involved anyway.",
				"Enjoy yourselves."
